<p>Baltimore doesn't get the attention that DC or Philadelphia do, and that's part of the opportunity. Housing costs are lower than both, the city is compact enough to cross in 20 minutes outside rush hour, and the demand drivers are steady: a world-famous hospital system, two pro stadiums downtown, a busy port and airport, and block after block of rowhomes that always need something. The best side hustles in Baltimore plug into those engines.</p>
<p>Here are 18 side jobs in Baltimore with typical pay, startup costs and local tips, plus the Maryland and Baltimore City tax rules you should know before your first 1099 arrives.</p>

<div class="stat-row">
  <div class="stat"><b>3.2%</b><span>Baltimore City local income tax</span></div>
